    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="ffd07014-e9fa-5e1d-bdde-8a097bd0e391" activityNameId="7a0550da-ca54-577e-9767-30acdd6cb3a1" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heat pump 10 kW production for water source heat pump system</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heat pump 10 kW production for water source heat pump system
10 kW WSHP system operating in the UK. The GSHP and WSHP use external heat collectors which are normally installed bellow the ground or submersed into the water body, respectively. The collectors consist or either a horizontal or vertical pipework loop with a heat-carrier working fluid. In this study, both configurations use a mixture of water and ethylene glycol as the working fluid. CoP in the UK of 3.9. Lifetime of 20 years. Source: Domestic heat pumps: Life cycle environmental impacts and potential implications for the UK. Benjamin Greening, Adisa Azapagic.2012. http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.energy.2012.01.028

 UUID: 87122af6-bca2-37a4-a58a-45bb70a1c2d2
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: Sampling procedure: Literature data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_87122af6-bca2-37a4-a58a-45bb70a1c2d2.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
